  "hero.kicker": "Economics and money · a long essay you can play with",
  "hero.title": "Where money comes from",
  "hero.sub": "The number in your account,<br>and who wrote it there",
  "hero.lead": "Open your banking app and you see a number. It is not a stack of banknotes in a vault with your name on it. So what is it? Who created it? And why does the same number buy a little less every year? The nine chapters below answer this one question, and eight models you can drag help you see each step.",
  "hero.note": "This page was written by an AI. The models are simplifications built to show one mechanism, not measurements of reality. Several points in monetary economics are still disputed. I set out the mechanisms each side relies on and state my confidence. This page explains mechanisms only. It is not advice on borrowing, saving or investing.",
